# Encrypted Card Flow (PCI)

This document provides a simple guide for integrating Tap Payments into both web and mobile applications, specifically tailored for PCI compliant merchants. It includes detailed instructions for encrypting cardholder data and processing payments securely. Merchants who are PCI compliant can encrypt the raw card data on their end and pass it to the Tap API for seamless payment processing.

# Card Encryption

To ensure security, card details must be encrypted using the RSA algorithm provided by Tap. Here is the tap [test encryption keys](https://developers.tap.company/reference/testing-keys). We highly recommend to use your own encryption keys from your merchant account.

```json RSA Key

```

**Secret Key**

```json Secret Key
sk_test_XKokBfNWv6FIYuTMg5sLPjhJ
```

Note: This is a test secret key which matches with the above RSA key. For your integration, please use your own secret key.

**Merchant ID**

```json Merchant ID
599424
```

Note: This is the Tap test Merchant ID. For your integration, please use your own Merchant ID.

Below are the steps to encrypt card information.

## Obtain the RSA Public Key from tap

Upon you submit your PCI and AOC certificate, tap will issue an RSA public key to perform the encryption. You can get the RSA Public Key from the tap Team.

## Prepare Data for Encryption

Ensure the card information is in JSON format:

```json json
{  
  "number": "5123450000000008",  
  "exp_month": "01",  
  "exp_year": "2039",  
  "cvc": "100",  
  "name": "test user"  
}
```

## Encrypt Card Information using RSA public key

Encrypt the JSON data using the RSA public key. The encrypted card is now ready to be sent in the API request.

```text Public key
-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----

-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
```

### Example Of The Encryption Function

```javascript
function encryptWithRSA(value, publicKey) {
  const valueString = JSON.stringify(value);
  const encrypted = crypto.publicEncrypt(
    {
      key: publicKey,
      padding: crypto.constants.RSA_PKCS1_PADDING
    },
    Buffer.from(valueString, 'utf-8')
  );

  return encrypted.toString('base64');
}

```
```java
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import java.security.KeyFactory;
import java.security.PublicKey;
import java.security.interfaces.RSAPublicKey;
import java.util.Base64;
import java.security.spec.X509EncodedKeySpec;

public class RSAEncryption {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            // JSON object to encrypt
            String objectToEncrypt = "{\n" +
                    "  \"number\": \"5123450000000008\",\n" +
                    "  \"exp_month\": \"01\",\n" +
                    "  \"exp_year\": \"2039\",\n" +
                    "  \"cvc\": \"100\",\n" +
                    "  \"name\": \"test user\"\n" +
                    "}";

            // Replace with your actual RSA public key (without BEGIN and END markers)
            String publicKeyBase64 = "";

            // Convert the Base64 public key to PublicKey object
            PublicKey publicKey = getPublicKeyFromBase64(publicKeyBase64);

            // Encrypt the object (JSON String)
            String encryptedValue = encryptWithRSA(objectToEncrypt, publicKey);
            System.out.println("Encrypted Value: " + encryptedValue);

        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }

    // Method to convert a Base64 string to an RSA public key
    public static PublicKey getPublicKeyFromBase64(String base64Key) throws Exception {
        byte[] decodedKey = Base64.getDecoder().decode(base64Key);
        X509EncodedKeySpec keySpec = new X509EncodedKeySpec(decodedKey);
        KeyFactory keyFactory = KeyFactory.getInstance("RSA");
        return keyFactory.generatePublic(keySpec);
    }

    // Method to encrypt a string using RSA public key
    public static String encryptWithRSA(String plainText, PublicKey publicKey) throws Exception {
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("RSA");
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, publicKey);

        byte[] encryptedBytes = cipher.doFinal(plainText.getBytes());
        return Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(encryptedBytes);
    }
}

```
```php
<?php

// The public key in PEM format (with BEGIN and END markers)
$publicKeyPEM = "
-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----

-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
";

// The JSON object to encrypt
$jsonObject = '{
  "number": "5123450000000008",
  "exp_month": "01",
  "exp_year": "2039",
  "cvc": "100",
  "name": "test user"
}';

// Convert PEM format public key to OpenSSL resource
$pubKey = openssl_pkey_get_public($publicKeyPEM);

// Check if the public key is valid
if (!$pubKey) {
    die("Invalid public key.");
}

// Encrypt the JSON object using RSA public key
if (openssl_public_encrypt($jsonObject, $encryptedData, $pubKey)) {
    // Base64 encode the encrypted data to make it readable
    $encryptedBase64 = base64_encode($encryptedData);
    echo "Encrypted Value: " . $encryptedBase64;
} else {
    echo "Encryption failed.";
}

?>

